1. Introduction

This Privacy Policy explains how the Bot ("Bot") collects, uses, stores, and protects information when used within the Discord server Thorium Beta.

By using the Bot, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.

2. Scope

This Privacy Policy applies only to the Bot's operation within the Discord server Thorium Beta.

The Bot is not intended for use outside of Thorium Beta.

3. Information Collected

The Bot may collect and process information necessary to provide its functionality, including:

Discord User IDs
Discord Server IDs
Channel IDs
Command usage
Messages submitted directly to the Bot
Conversation content provided to the Bot
Configuration and preference data
System logs and diagnostic information

The Bot does not intentionally collect more information than necessary for its operation.

4. AI Training and User Consent

The Bot may use conversations, prompts, messages, feedback, and interactions within Thorium Beta to improve, develop, evaluate, or train AI systems.

However:

AI training will only occur with the user's permission.
Users may decline participation in AI training.
Refusing permission will not affect access to the Bot's standard features unless a feature specifically requires data contribution.
Permission may be requested through commands, forms, settings, or other mechanisms provided by the Bot administrators.

If a user does not provide consent, their content will not be intentionally used for AI training purposes.

5. How Information Is Used

Information may be used to:

Operate the Bot
Respond to commands and requests
Improve performance and reliability
Fix bugs and technical issues
Prevent abuse or misuse
Maintain security
Develop and improve AI-powered features where consent has been granted
6. Data Sharing

The Bot does not sell user information.

Information may only be shared when:

Required by applicable law.
Necessary to protect the security or integrity of the Bot.
Required to investigate abuse, fraud, or violations of the Terms of Service.
Authorized by the user.
7. Data Retention

Data will be retained only for as long as reasonably necessary to:

Operate the Bot.
Maintain records related to consent.
Improve services.
Meet legal or security requirements.

Data may be deleted, anonymized, or aggregated at the discretion of the Bot owner.

8. User Rights

Users may request:

Information about data collected about them.
Correction of inaccurate information.
Withdrawal of previously granted AI-training consent.
Deletion of eligible stored data, where technically feasible and legally permitted.

Requests should be directed to the Bot administrators within Thorium Beta.

9. Security

Reasonable measures are taken to protect information from unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction.

However, no system can guarantee absolute security.

10. Children's Privacy

The Bot is not directed toward individuals under the minimum age required to use Discord under applicable laws and Discord's Terms of Service.

11. Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be modified at any time.

Continued use of the Bot after changes become effective constitutes acceptance of the updated Privacy Policy.

12. Contact

Questions regarding this Privacy Policy should be directed to the Bot owner or administrators within the Thorium Beta Discord server.

Consent Notice

By explicitly opting in, users may allow their interactions with the Bot in Thorium Beta to be used for AI training, improvement, evaluation, and development purposes. Users who do not provide consent will not have their content intentionally included in AI training datasets.
